<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="095f-2e2b" project="ebilling-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Internal Correction path (B′), client: "Submit corrected invoice" on Invoice Review opens the Create Invoice wizard in Correction mode</title>
    <phase>5 Review — 095f part 2 (EB-D-243, EB-D-245)</phase>
    <gate>095f-2e2a merged into work. Branch from work/ebilling-r1 at the sha named in the agent brief.</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Shared UI library change (InvoiceSubmissionWizard, used by the external SPA) plus a code page; tests modified.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>095f-2e2a</deps>
    <tags>react, fluent-ui, frontend, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1 day</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Implement the client half of option B′ (projects/ebilling-r1/notes/095f-part2-decision-notes-design.md §16, §13; EB-D-245). Invoice Review (src/solutions/InvoiceReview) gets a "Submit corrected invoice" action for an invoice that is In Review. It opens the Create Invoice wizard (src/solutions/CreateInvoiceWizard, which hosts the shared InvoiceSubmissionWizard in Spaarke.UI.Components) with a new optional `correction` prop: the firm invoice number prefilled from GET /api/finance/invoices/{id}/correction-prefill, the record locked, and a required note box (the shared note rules and NoteField pattern). The wizard posts the internal multipart route with mode=Correction, invoiceId and correctionNote (095f-2e2a's contract).</prompt>

  <goal>A reviewer can replace an In Review invoice with a corrected PDF from Invoice Review, and the replacement goes through the same checks as every other Correction.</goal>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spa-r4 condition 1">Without `correction` the wizard behaves byte-for-byte as today, proven by the existing suites unchanged, including InvoiceSubmissionWizard.lockedRecord.test.tsx.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spa-r4 condition 2">It composes with lockedRecord, hideTitle and the submittingRef close guard; state whether correction + lockedRecord is supported or refused, and test it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spa-r4 condition 3">A minor version bump of Spaarke.UI.Components (3.x), with consumer lockfiles refreshed in the same change.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spa-r4 condition 4">spa-r4 does a scoped diff review before the change merges (the coordinator sends it).</constraint>
    <constraint source="EB-D-245">The action shows only for an invoice that is In Review; the server still decides eligibility, and each refusal code (no note, 404, 409 CorrectionNotAllowed) shows a plain message.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Fluent v9 tokens only; dark mode.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Only src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components (the wizard and its tests), src/solutions/CreateInvoiceWizard, src/solutions/InvoiceReview, consumer lockfiles, and a notes file. No server change, no deploy.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Jest: with `correction` the wizard prefills the number, locks the record, requires the note and posts mode, invoiceId and correctionNote; without it every existing wizard test passes unchanged (must-not-fire).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Jest: Invoice Review shows the action only for In Review, opens the wizard with the correction, refreshes after success, and shows each refusal message.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Jest: the submit is disabled while a request is in flight; a double click sends exactly one Correction (095f-2e2a K2: two Corrections of one invoice can both be received, and the second fails at commit).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The shared library, CreateInvoiceWizard, InvoiceReview and external-spa Jest suites are green; npm run typecheck and npm run build succeed for each.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
  </execution>
</task>
